<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com - Top Stories</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:55:00Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-top" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-top" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Trump escalates trade war with Canada with import bans, 50% tariffs</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cf5c7cd94bf29a431d1718609a6a59461b3bd19207ab7a941fc31a8856f93309</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:54:55Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T03:10:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/trump-escalates-trade-war-with-canada-with-import-bans-50-tariffs/a-79195010--753932b9b85d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/trump-escalates-trade-war-with-canada-with-import-bans-50-tariffs/a-79195010?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">US President Trump has announced new import bans and 50% tariffs on some Canadian goods as tensions between the two countries intensify. This comes a day after Ottawa's retaliatory tariffs on US products took effect.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Israel's Netanyahu denies UAE warned him of October 7 attack</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c55c47783a5e78669b1628e145afacac5789ca135ffe8db9eb423c6bb8feae80</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:54:58Z</updated><published>2026-09-09T00:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/israel-s-netanyahu-denies-uae-warned-him-of-october-7-attack/a-79194436--3205edb6ce2a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/israel-s-netanyahu-denies-uae-warned-him-of-october-7-attack/a-79194436?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Israeli media reported that the UAE contacted Israeli Prime Minister Netanyahu before the October 7, 2023 attacks, warning him that Hamas was planning a major operation. The prime minister has rejected the reports.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>US strikes oil tankers off coast of Iran</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:154d298ad5ffbf6af3b6aed7da44b26e359721ec984c01abc731e33565e40058</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:55:00Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T21:56:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-strikes-oil-tankers-off-coast-of-iran/a-79194562--b1b4c69892f6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-strikes-oil-tankers-off-coast-of-iran/a-79194562?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The US attacked four oil-carrying vessels in the Gulf of Oman and one in the Strait of Hormuz. Iran's Revolutionary Guard said it would strike ships off Bahrain and Kuwait in retaliation.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>German economy frets about Saxony-Anhalt election results</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:53df2fc1cd7b676ad6382fda945951ed2e244b717b41bc2b2e35b676c1ac5e45</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:53:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T18:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-economy-frets-about-saxony-anhalt-election-results/a-79162871--94d137604c23.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-economy-frets-about-saxony-anhalt-election-results/a-79162871?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The AfD won the election in the eastern German state by a wide margin. While politicians and election analysts are still debating the reasons for the far-right party's popularity, economists are sounding the alarm.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>EU, UK express dismay over Mladic funeral in Serbia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2e819766332e5c0d3e17296bffbea7487864c96be4e4583dbdc9beeb728450aa</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:53:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T16:52:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-uk-express-dismay-over-mladic-funeral-in-serbia/a-79190233--29af1d88dc44.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-uk-express-dismay-over-mladic-funeral-in-serbia/a-79190233?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The EU is deliberating an official response to the glorification of war criminal Ratko Mladic in Belgrade. The UK, meanwhile, summoned Serbia's charge d'affaires over the display.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Fifty years after Mao’s death, China has transformed. DW looks at why his political legacy still matters.</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3547e2b655a2fb9ff044ee91a239b4572688c5e7cd87ab473b5e3db784e225b6</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:53:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T14:44:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/fifty-years-after-mao-s-death-china-has-transformed-dw-looks-at-why-his-political-legacy-still-matte/a-79189751--6efb4c761178.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/fifty-years-after-mao-s-death-china-has-transformed-dw-looks-at-why-his-political-legacy-still-matters/a-79189751?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Mao Zedong was perhaps the most influential, and certainly one of the most controversial, figures in 20th-century China. Even five decades after his death, the legacy of his era continues to influence China today.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Ratko Mladic’s funeral casts shadow over Bosnia and Herzegovina vote</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f71e3c489f5f1cc6a5ee208e77b84363149d9d37ca71aefd8cd82997f28de1de</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:53:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T14:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ratko-mladic-s-funeral-casts-shadow-over-bosnia-and-herzegovina-vote/a-79189319--342fd5cbe6c7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ratko-mladic-s-funeral-casts-shadow-over-bosnia-and-herzegovina-vote/a-79189319?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Ratko Mladic’s funeral in Belgrade, attended by Serbian and Bosnian Serb leaders, has deepened regional tensions and could affect the upcoming election in Bosnia and Herzegovina.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>BSW and AfD – a political love-hate relationship in Germany</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c36472c243ba74ffa4bf782044621b6dea97672bc93957542f0870a70a4e3e2e</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:53:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T13:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bsw-and-afd-a-political-love-hate-relationship-in-germany/a-79185782--2f6a7962abcf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bsw-and-afd-a-political-love-hate-relationship-in-germany/a-79185782?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Sahra Wagenknecht Alliance (BSW) could help the Alternative for Germany (AfD) into power in Saxony-Anhalt. But the BSW is riddled with infighting</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>EU court rules against Belgian far-right party in IKEA case</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d9477e3f054d80ddf5197ca8117dfed6e14df4d4f7897a9a4e8288497ab7a5a1</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:53:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T12:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-court-rules-against-belgian-far-right-party-in-ikea-case/a-79159207--531c0db38ccd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-court-rules-against-belgian-far-right-party-in-ikea-case/a-79159207?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A European court has backed Ikea's challenge against a Belgian far-right party, saying the use of Ikea-style visuals could harm the company's reputation.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>UK announces trade sanctions on Israeli settlements in occupied West Bank</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f3602a38852bb8ffd950e69c683c0a7b1fbf88a9a789379e1d529c5549b34b55</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:53:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T12:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uk-announces-trade-sanctions-on-israeli-settlements-in-occupied-west-bank/a-79155051--d2a4da122a4f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uk-announces-trade-sanctions-on-israeli-settlements-in-occupied-west-bank/a-79155051?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Foreign Secretary Ed Miliband said the measures were in response to what he called "settler terrorism" in the occupied territories. The measures are part of the UK's efforts to support a two-state solution.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Japan's empty temples seek new ways to survive</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ca0cfcf36c5bc4f84d8e3bb792cf9e75d37763af79b620cb3bf8179c92605f82</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:53:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T12:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/japan-s-empty-temples-seek-new-ways-to-survive/a-79157964--7eea677a26bf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/japan-s-empty-temples-seek-new-ways-to-survive/a-79157964?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">With a declining population, shrinking congregations and growing economic pressures, temples are struggling to stay relevant. As more temples are sold or closed, is religion in decline in modern Japan?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Afghanistan's women: A national soccer team without a home</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fc2f00c3b2c32e0331e1ccd086e1be4a9f834ca7e998425558a097755c78a123</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:53:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T11:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/afghanistan-s-women-a-national-soccer-team-without-a-home/a-79139500--7cfb666b9c3a.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/afghanistan-s-women-a-national-soccer-team-without-a-home/a-79139500?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Afghan women's national football team has finally been officially recognized by FIFA. Now the players want to make history both on and off the field.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>German police arrest suspect in power grid sabotage case</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1a15b05b247fb8906720850b020946807e5ec08f1c899c476aaf230f7a756502</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:53:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T10:54:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-police-arrest-suspect-in-power-grid-sabotage-case/a-79161142--0b56d3da8acf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-police-arrest-suspect-in-power-grid-sabotage-case/a-79161142?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Investigators say the suspect used homemade rockets and conductive wire to target high-voltage lines in three German states, apparently as part of a campaign against fossil fuels.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Hungary orders 10 Russian diplomats to leave</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2abf0df5ed4bb84559aac3e060282f781adde037d182beecec67da346bd734ca</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:53:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T10:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/hungary-orders-10-russian-diplomats-to-leave/a-79157576--560dc3bd8df1.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/hungary-orders-10-russian-diplomats-to-leave/a-79157576?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Budapest says the expulsions are necessary to protect security and sovereignty after years of comparatively close ties between Hungary and Russia.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>US-Canada tariff dispute weighs on cross-border ties</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:53dc2dae2464aa823232983c17807900bb74ab8c4e872fe1f0b66a3aa479cb92</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:53:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T10:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-canada-tariff-dispute-weighs-on-cross-border-ties/a-78815803--082b25646c1e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-canada-tariff-dispute-weighs-on-cross-border-ties/a-78815803?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As Canada's retaliatory tariffs take effect, Canadian and US car industries fear the trade war will hit them hard, while Canadians are cutting back on travel.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Kenya: Crackdown on foreign traders prompts xenophobia fears</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a88bafdd5aebe7c65fe24802696de5dcd18852659fc9ab8d179590234949b5af</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:53:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T09:14:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/kenya-crackdown-on-foreign-traders-prompts-xenophobia-fears/a-79143847--a8e571d0a365.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/kenya-crackdown-on-foreign-traders-prompts-xenophobia-fears/a-79143847?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Concerns about xenophobia are rising in Kenya after President William Ruto ordered a crackdown on foreigners working as hawkers. The government insists however that legally documented foreign traders remain protected.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Australia targets big tech with algorithm opt-out bill</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:22427ba0a88e939d4749be28ce281250c7fc1ba8314d0e08f11009375a7d62a5</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:53:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T09:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/australia-targets-big-tech-with-algorithm-opt-out-bill/a-79154108--95b8ccd62504.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/australia-targets-big-tech-with-algorithm-opt-out-bill/a-79154108?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The "My Feed, My Way," legislation would require the likes of Facebook, TikTok and Instagram to let users opt out of algorithms or risk heavy fines.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Renoir Museum robbery: 2 paintings missing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9f69673c64f9cd097e4f92101ba305e13b9c1c970732bc8d18389f1d1e82b0b3</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:53:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T07:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/renoir-museum-robbery-2-paintings-missing/a-79154458--4fcf4fff5ab0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/renoir-museum-robbery-2-paintings-missing/a-79154458?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Police are on the hunt for thieves who stole two paintings from the Renoir Museum on the French Riviera in an overnight heist. Two other stolen works were abandoned as they fled.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>PISA test reveals alarming drop in reading and math skills</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:06469bd2e9ada99f65d8e526eb62235515409d7b3b01cd2bf132a53fae3337d6</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:53:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T07:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/pisa-test-reveals-alarming-drop-in-reading-and-math-skills/a-79147293--6fcb0a53f051.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/pisa-test-reveals-alarming-drop-in-reading-and-math-skills/a-79147293?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The 2025 results from the influential global study show a downward trend in students' performance. Germany's 15-year-olds are faring worse than ever.</summary><category term="Culture" /></entry><entry><title>Elversberg: Bundesliga newcomers from tiny town make waves</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8c4b47a05084c4b8e2c0c44b0fd9b009ac48bcba75e34fe488404efaf9b4a615</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:53:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T06:47:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/elversberg-bundesliga-newcomers-from-tiny-town-make-waves/a-77194483--9d72d35ebb6f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/elversberg-bundesliga-newcomers-from-tiny-town-make-waves/a-77194483?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A team from a small southwestern German town of just 7,000 inhabitants made history by sealing promotion to become the 59th club to play in the Bundesliga. Elversberg has got off to a memorable start.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Female footballers offered egg freezing but doubts remain</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f8760aa1710067e64f73a8221428abc8c638206425ebae93027857bfcef966da</id><updated>2026-09-09T04:53:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-08T06:45:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/female-footballers-offered-egg-freezing-but-doubts-remain/a-79145259--e96625275f81.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/female-footballers-offered-egg-freezing-but-doubts-remain/a-79145259?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Spain's football federation are set to join a handful of clubs in paying for female players to freeze their eggs during their careers. While players have pushed for the move, there are welfare concerns too.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry></feed>
